{
  "_how": "The hero's layers, in reference.png pixel space (2000x1116); the render is out_scale times that. Layers draw in z order, low first. A can: `product` is the packshot, cx/cy its centre, `width` its body width, `tilt` degrees (positive = the can's bottom swings right). `native_*` describe the packshot as delivered: an upright front-on can is tilt 0 and its PNG width; one shot at an angle gives its own tilt, body width and body length. A sprite is a cut-out from source/sprites/: x/y its top-left, `flip` mirrors it, and `tuck` names the can its sliced side hides behind — compose.py slides it sideways until that edge is covered, so x is a starting point. `pending` lists where the reference had the products still to come. `email_crop` is the x range (reference pixels) kept for the 600px email version.",
